cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "CAISO and ERCOT Battery Energy Storage Case Studies"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
abstract: >-
  Code, prepared inputs, supplied model outputs, and figure workflows for battery
  energy storage case studies in the CAISO and ERCOT electricity markets. The
  CAISO case covers January 2023 through December 2025 and compares historical
  fleet operation with bidding and self-scheduling strategies. The ERCOT case
  covers January through June 2026, with 13 configured storage resources and
  system-impact estimates under gas, coal, and combined thermal displacement
  assumptions. The cases use separate Python environments; optimization requires
  a separately licensed Gurobi installation. ERCOT upstream acquisition and
  complete fuel-stack construction are outside the distributed workflow. The
  MIT License applies to original software and its documentation only; data,
  results, figures, and third-party materials are subject to the rights boundaries
  in DATA_AND_THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the ERCOT provenance note.

